    "content": "On July 10, 2025, the Somali Federal Cabinet approved the formation of the National Higher Education Commission, a 15-member body tasked with regulating and improving higher education across the country. Dr. Cabdinuur Sheekh Maxamed, a former Minister of Education, was appointed as its first chairperson.\n\nExactly one year later, the cabinet removed Dr. Cabdinuur from his role and appointed Dr. Maxamuud Axmed Jimcaale as the new chair. The reasons for the leadership change have not been officially detailed, but it comes amid ongoing efforts to reform Somalia's higher education sector, which has faced challenges including quality control and accreditation.\n\nThe commission's responsibilities include setting academic standards, accrediting universities, and ensuring that institutions meet national requirements. For the Somali diaspora, the commission's performance is of particular interest because many diaspora families invest in higher education back home and rely on recognized qualifications for their children's future.\n\nDr. Maxamuud Axmed Jimcaale now leads the commission at a critical time, as the body works to establish credibility and implement policies that can elevate the quality of Somali universities. Observers will be watching whether the change in leadership signals a shift in strategy or priorities.\n\nThe government has not announced further changes to the commission's membership, and the body continues its mandate to oversee the nation's higher education landscape.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/07/23/qiimayn-muxuu-yahay-guddiga-tacliinta-sare-ee-qaranka-maxaase-u-qabsoomay-muddadii-sannadka-ahayd-ee-uu-jiray/",
